---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { DIGUP_UI } from '../../lib/site';
---
<Layout
  title={'DigUp FAQ — Requirements, Privacy, Platforms, Troubleshooting'}
  description={'DigUp FAQ: Apple Silicon vs Windows/Linux beta, model size, privacy (local-first), brew install, indexing time, code search, and links to official GitHub Releases.'}
  canonicalPath="/faq/"
  lang="en"
  ogImage={DIGUP_UI.audio.src}
>
  <main class="wrap">
    <header class="page-hero">
      <p class="meta-line"><span class="badge">FAQ</span> · Common questions</p>
      <h1>DigUp FAQ</h1>
      <p class="lead">Short answers with links to thicker guides. Always prefer official GitHub README and Releases when anything conflicts.</p>
    </header>

    <article class="wide">
      <div class="cta-bar">
        <a class="cta" href="https://github.com/ylwl1997/digup-run-app/releases" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Releases</a>
        <a class="cta-secondary" href="/what-is-digup/">What is DigUp?</a>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item" id="official">
        <h2>Is digup.run the official DigUp website?</h2>
        <p><strong>No.</strong> digup.run is the <strong>Digup Run</strong> product site. Digup Run is based on DigUp (MIT) and is <strong>not</strong> an official DigUp / ARahim3 product. Downloads ship from <a href="https://github.com/ylwl1997/digup-run-app/releases" rel="noopener noreferrer">ylwl1997/digup-run-app Releases</a>. Upstream DigUp: <a href="https://github.com/ARahim3/DigUp" rel="noopener noreferrer">ARahim3/DigUp</a>.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item" id="platforms">
        <h2>Which platforms are supported?</h2>
        <p>Mac: <strong>0.6.1</strong> stable on Apple Silicon, macOS 14+. Windows and Linux: <strong>0.7.0-beta.1</strong> beta on 64-bit Intel/AMD. See <a href="/install-mac/">Mac</a>, <a href="/install-windows/">Windows</a>, and <a href="/install-linux/">Linux</a> guides. Re-check Releases before you install.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item" id="intel-mac">
        <h2>Does DigUp run on Intel Macs?</h2>
        <p>The Digup Run Mac build targets <strong>Apple Silicon</strong> only. Intel Macs are not supported by that build. Use Windows/Linux beta on compatible PCs if you need those platforms instead.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item" id="privacy">
        <h2>Is DigUp private? Is there telemetry or an account?</h2>
        <p>DigUp is designed local-first: indexing and inference run on your machine. Upstream documents no account requirement and no telemetry of your file contents. Expect a first model download and optional update checks you can control. Read the current README privacy section for the definitive wording.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item" id="model-size">
        <h2>How big is the model download?</h2>
        <p>About <strong>865 MB</strong> on first run (EmbeddingGemma 2 via llama.cpp). On Mac 0.6.1, if the network blocks the download, use Settings → Storage → <strong>Use Files…</strong>. Details: <a href="/embeddinggemma-2/">EmbeddingGemma 2 in DigUp</a>.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item" id="indexing">
        <h2>How long does indexing take?</h2>
        <p>Depends on folder size, file types, and CPU/GPU. DigUp shows an estimate after a quick speed check. After the first pass, new files are indexed incrementally. You can schedule indexing hours on Mac (0.6.1 Settings → Folders).</p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item" id="brew">
        <h2>Homebrew or DMG on Mac?</h2>
        <p>Use the Mac DMG from <a href="https://github.com/ylwl1997/digup-run-app/releases">ylwl1997/digup-run-app Releases</a> (Homebrew cask not published yet). Step-by-step: <a href="/install-mac/">Install Digup Run on Mac</a>.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item" id="beta">
        <h2>What does “beta” mean for Windows and Linux?</h2>
        <p>0.7.0-beta.1 works but has had far less real-world use than Mac. Expect rough edges. Screenshot OCR text is not in yet; .doc / RAW / SVG are skipped on that beta. Prefer filing issues upstream with logs (e.g. <code>speed.log</code> device line).</p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item" id="code">
        <h2>How does code search work?</h2>
        <p>Code indexing is optional — enable it in settings and select repositories. Query with the <code>code:</code> prefix. DigUp is not a full IDE replacement; it jumps to matching lines when code search is enabled.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item" id="spotlight">
        <h2>Should I turn off Spotlight if I install DigUp?</h2>
        <p>No need. DigUp is additive. Keep Spotlight for names and apps; use DigUp for meaning across modalities. See <a href="/vs-spotlight/">DigUp vs Spotlight</a>.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item" id="smartscreen">
        <h2>Windows says it doesn’t recognize DigUp. Is that normal?</h2>
        <p>The beta installer is <strong>unsigned</strong>. SmartScreen may require More info → Run anyway. Only do this for the EXE you downloaded from the official ARahim3 Releases page. Guide: <a href="/install-windows/">Install on Windows</a>.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item" id="stars">
        <h2>How popular is the project?</h2>
        <p>As of 2026-10-15 the GitHub API reported about <strong>3,716</strong> stars and 252 forks, with Mac 0.6.1 and Win/Linux 0.7.0-beta.1 published. Live counts change — check the repo.</p>
      </div>

      <h2 style="margin-top:2rem;">Quick requirements table</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Platform</th><th>Version</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Mac</td><td>0.6.1</td><td>Apple Silicon, macOS 14+</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Windows</td><td>0.7.0-beta.1</td><td>64-bit 10/11, unsigned setup</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Linux</td><td>0.7.0-beta.1</td><td>.deb / AppImage amd64</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <div class="cta-bar">
        <a class="cta" href="https://github.com/ylwl1997/digup-run-app/releases" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Releases</a>
        <a class="cta-secondary" href="/changelog-notes/">Changelog notes</a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
